WEBVTT

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.274
♪ ♪

00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:25.651
(flames roaring)

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:27.611
(girl panting)

00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:29.864
(explosion)

00:00:36.704 --> 00:00:39.707
-Close the valves!
-The fire is coming around, hurry!

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.792
(workers shouting indistinctly)

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:47.882
(girl gasps)

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:52.261
-There she is!
-She has the flower seeds.

00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:54.513
Don't let her get away!

00:00:54.597 --> 00:00:57.099
♪ ♪

00:00:58.392 --> 00:01:01.395
(explosion booming)

00:01:19.497 --> 00:01:21.874
Woman:
Don't just stand there, get her!

00:01:42.061 --> 00:01:44.063
(gasping)

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.236
(screams)

00:01:55.241 --> 00:01:57.243
♪ ♪

00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:33.654
(squawking)

00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:49.587
♪ ♪

00:02:50.004 --> 00:02:53.757
MARY AND THE WITCH'S FLOWER

00:03:10.566 --> 00:03:11.650
Hmm?

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.702
(groaning)

00:03:22.745 --> 00:03:25.623
Mary:
Aah! I'm so bored.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.627
Miss Banks:
Mary, have you finished unpacking?

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:33.839
Ah, unpacking, yes!

00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:36.508
(grunts)

00:03:37.843 --> 00:03:39.720
-(tape rips)
-(gasps)

00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:41.138
Oh, no!

00:03:42.014 --> 00:03:45.267
Well, that's one box unpacked at least.

00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:56.612
Hi, I'm Mary Smith, and I'm
starting at your school today.

00:03:59.073 --> 00:04:00.491
(sighs)

00:04:04.536 --> 00:04:06.372
I hate my hair.

00:04:06.455 --> 00:04:07.623
Eee!

00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:11.210
Miss Banks:
She's ready, come on down!

00:04:11.335 --> 00:04:12.378
Coming!

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.218
I wonder if she has finished unpacking.

00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:21.011
Miss Banks:
Oh, I doubt it.

00:04:21.095 --> 00:04:24.431
Last time I cleaned in there,
those boxes were still untouched.

00:04:24.515 --> 00:04:27.017
(footsteps stomping)

00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:31.188
Nearly done with my unpacking,
Great Aunt Charlotte.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.690
Good girl.

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:35.526
-Hello, Miss Banks, let me help.
-(yelps)

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:36.777
(sighs)

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:39.238
That's all right, love.

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:42.866
We have somewhere
very important to go today, Mary.

00:04:42.992 --> 00:04:45.119
-Great.
-Oh...

00:04:45.244 --> 00:04:47.204
I'd love to come, I can help.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.415
(gasps)

00:04:51.917 --> 00:04:53.919
(whimpering)

00:04:54.003 --> 00:04:54.837
Oh, dear.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.715
I'm really sorry.

00:04:59.008 --> 00:05:02.094
Don't worry, you don't have to help out.
That's my job.

00:05:04.054 --> 00:05:07.599
-Oh.
-(Charlotte chuckles)

00:05:07.683 --> 00:05:09.018
Please, allow me.

00:05:10.686 --> 00:05:12.271
Charlotte:
Thank you, dear.

00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:17.943
So where are we going today,
somewhere nice, somewhere interesting?

00:05:19.111 --> 00:05:22.698
I'm so excited.
Will there be other kids to play with?

00:05:22.781 --> 00:05:25.034
(laughs nervously)

00:05:25.117 --> 00:05:27.786
Sorry, dear, it's a funeral,
forgot to say.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.831
Oh, so I won't be coming with you?

00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:36.128
We'll be back by six,
perhaps another day we'll go out.

00:05:36.211 --> 00:05:38.630
Now you can watch TV until we're back.

00:05:38.756 --> 00:05:41.216
-Mary: But it's broken.
-Eh?

00:05:45.095 --> 00:05:47.473
-(banging)
-Oh my, you're right.

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:51.852
-We should probably get that looked at.
-Charlotte: Mm, yes, we should.

00:05:52.644 --> 00:05:56.607
Oh by, the way, your parents
called earlier, Mary.

00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:58.358
Really, are they coming soon?

00:05:58.484 --> 00:06:00.235
Miss Banks:
They're not quite finished with work yet,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.447
so it will be a little while longer
before they can come.

00:06:03.489 --> 00:06:04.490
Oh, I see.

00:06:05.407 --> 00:06:08.160
It's a good thing you
came here ahead of them.

00:06:08.911 --> 00:06:12.081
If you'd have come with them,
you'd have started school later

00:06:12.164 --> 00:06:13.874
than everybody else, wouldn't you?

00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:17.169
-(dog whining)
-But there's still a week left.

00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:18.921
Miss Banks:
It will fly by.

00:06:19.004 --> 00:06:22.257
Once summer break's over,
the kids will be back

00:06:22.341 --> 00:06:25.552
and Redmanor Village will be swarming
with the little blighters again.

00:06:25.636 --> 00:06:28.806
I'll die of boredom first probably.

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:30.599
(dog yawns)

00:06:30.682 --> 00:06:33.018
-Hmm?
-Here, I made you a picnic.

00:06:33.102 --> 00:06:34.853
It's the perfect day to get out.

00:06:34.937 --> 00:06:36.647
Oh, thank you, Miss Banks.

00:06:37.356 --> 00:06:41.068
I'm sorry, Mary, we'll be sure to be
back home by supper.

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:42.027
Okay.

00:06:42.111 --> 00:06:44.530
-(clattering)
-Hmm?

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:49.993
Look, there's Zebedee!

00:06:50.077 --> 00:06:51.954
I'll go and see if he needs any help.

00:06:52.037 --> 00:06:54.123
Don't get in the way
of his work now, Mary.

00:06:54.206 --> 00:06:55.582
No, I won't.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.669
Confucius, are you coming?

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.507
(Confucius grumbles)

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.051
I'll take that as a no then.

00:07:06.135 --> 00:07:07.970
See you later.

00:07:08.053 --> 00:07:09.888
Charlotte:
Have fun, Mary.

00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:13.058
Miss Banks:
Will you look at her go?

00:07:13.142 --> 00:07:15.227
You're meant to look
twice before you leap.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.563
-She hardly looks at all.
-(Charlotte chuckles)

00:07:18.272 --> 00:07:20.983
That's what I love most
about her, Miss Banks.

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:26.989
Zebedee?

00:07:28.574 --> 00:07:29.867
Hello?

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.577
Where did he go?

00:07:31.702 --> 00:07:32.703
-(leaves rustle)
-(gasps)

00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:34.121
Zebedee.

00:07:36.415 --> 00:07:38.333
Something wrong?

00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:42.045
You made me jump, you just seemed to pop
out of the shrubbery.

00:07:42.129 --> 00:07:44.715
Zebedee:
A good gardener's part of the landscape.

00:07:50.304 --> 00:07:52.347
Can I help with that, can I?

00:07:53.765 --> 00:07:54.892
Hmm?

00:08:01.565 --> 00:08:02.900
Thank you, Zebedee.

00:08:06.737 --> 00:08:08.864
-You be careful with those now.
-Yes.

00:08:11.783 --> 00:08:12.951
(gasps)

00:08:14.244 --> 00:08:15.245
Oh, no.

00:08:15.329 --> 00:08:18.207
I'm very sorry.

00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:20.918
Never mind.

00:08:22.252 --> 00:08:25.380
Children and dogs just
aren't cut out for gardening.

00:08:32.971 --> 00:08:35.140
Mary:
A broomstick?

00:08:37.476 --> 00:08:38.977
All right.

00:08:40.812 --> 00:08:42.814
(Mary grunts)

00:08:42.856 --> 00:08:46.777
See, I knew I could do it.

00:08:48.946 --> 00:08:53.659
I just wish I had a smaller broomstick.

00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:56.286
-(thuds)
-(gasps)

00:08:59.665 --> 00:09:01.833
(Mary screaming)

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:05.003
-(muffled shouting)
-Huh?

00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:07.130
-(Mary grunting)
-Oh!

00:09:14.137 --> 00:09:16.348
(laughing)

00:09:17.432 --> 00:09:20.519
It's a person under there (laughs).

00:09:21.645 --> 00:09:25.524
Thought it was a monkey,
a red-haired monkey, covered in leaves.

00:09:25.607 --> 00:09:27.859
(laughing)

00:09:30.237 --> 00:09:33.407
That's nice. Didn't your parents
teach you any manners?

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.701
Oh, I'm supposed to deliver something.

00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:37.577
Hey, wait.

00:09:37.703 --> 00:09:39.288
Hello, Miss Banks.

00:09:40.414 --> 00:09:43.333
Hello, Peter, good to see you.

00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:44.793
Peter.

00:09:44.876 --> 00:09:46.712
Peter:
My mum wants me to bring these to you.

00:09:48.171 --> 00:09:52.050
That's very kind. Working hard instead
of having a holiday, are we?

00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:53.760
Yes, Mum needs all the help she can get.

00:09:53.885 --> 00:09:55.304
Miss Banks:
How is your mum, Peter?

00:09:55.387 --> 00:09:58.765
Peter: She's fine.
She'll be at the mayor's funeral.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:01.184
Oh, I look forward
to seeing her there then.

00:10:02.019 --> 00:10:05.856
Ah, Zebedee. Can you bring the car around?

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:16.074
Right here, you missed one.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.411
-(grumbles)
-See you later.

00:10:20.329 --> 00:10:22.539
Eee!

00:10:48.774 --> 00:10:50.484
(cat meows)

00:10:52.819 --> 00:10:54.404
Do you want some?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.285
Go on, it's nice.

00:11:05.832 --> 00:11:08.877
You know, I feel sorry for you,
being born a black cat.

00:11:09.002 --> 00:11:10.962
Everyone calling you unlucky.

00:11:11.004 --> 00:11:13.465
I can relate though.

00:11:14.174 --> 00:11:16.385
I've got this frizzy red hair,

00:11:16.468 --> 00:11:19.429
I've no friends to eat my lunch with.

00:11:21.807 --> 00:11:24.393
And I'm rubbish at absolutely everything.

00:11:25.519 --> 00:11:29.189
I doubt anything good
will ever happen in my life.

00:11:30.315 --> 00:11:32.401
(Mary sighs)

00:11:33.527 --> 00:11:34.694
Hmm?

00:11:36.613 --> 00:11:41.201
Hey wait. I haven't finished
complaining about my life.

00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:44.663
Mary:
Hmm?

00:11:45.539 --> 00:11:47.874
Weren't you just black?

00:12:02.305 --> 00:12:04.141
How did you do that?

00:12:08.562 --> 00:12:09.646
(gasps)

00:12:17.654 --> 00:12:19.948
I've never been in these woods before.

00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:22.534
Wait.

00:12:22.617 --> 00:12:24.953
I'll get lost if I lose sight of you.

00:12:28.582 --> 00:12:32.544
Slow down, you're going too fast.

00:12:40.385 --> 00:12:41.261
Huh?

00:12:50.854 --> 00:12:52.397
What happened here?

00:13:03.867 --> 00:13:08.371
Of course, there's two of you.
Look at that, you're a couple.

00:13:11.249 --> 00:13:12.375
Oh.

00:13:17.088 --> 00:13:20.008
(yowling)

00:13:20.133 --> 00:13:21.635
What's wrong?

00:13:26.431 --> 00:13:28.808
♪ ♪

00:13:32.103 --> 00:13:33.438
(gasps)

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:38.735
Beautiful.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:43.114
(cats yowling)

00:13:43.615 --> 00:13:45.534
I'm only taking one.

00:13:49.412 --> 00:13:50.789
Ah...

00:13:50.872 --> 00:13:53.166
What are you called, I wonder.

00:13:53.291 --> 00:13:55.961
-(yowling)
-I’ll ask Zebedee later.

00:13:58.964 --> 00:14:00.507
Isn't it lovely?

00:14:01.758 --> 00:14:03.301
I found it in the woods.

00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:07.472
I was following two cats,
a gray one and a black one.

00:14:07.597 --> 00:14:09.891
Hm, I wonder where they're from.

00:14:09.975 --> 00:14:13.144
The black one is Tib,
the gray one is Gib.

00:14:13.228 --> 00:14:16.189
They belong to that young lad, Peter.

00:14:17.607 --> 00:14:18.692
Peter?

00:14:19.734 --> 00:14:20.735
Aah, not him.

00:14:21.611 --> 00:14:25.740
Zebedee: The cats don't really belong
to any one, of course.

00:14:26.491 --> 00:14:28.577
I must say, I'm surprised you found this

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:33.039
on your first trip
to the forest, young lady.

00:14:34.165 --> 00:14:36.793
That flower's called a fly-by-night.

00:14:36.918 --> 00:14:41.006
-Fly-by-night?
-Mm. That's the most common name.

00:14:41.089 --> 00:14:43.800
Though she's anything but common.

00:14:44.676 --> 00:14:49.347
They only grow in these woods, and
they only bloom once every seven years.

00:14:49.389 --> 00:14:54.060
In fact, this is the first time
I've seen one.

00:14:54.185 --> 00:14:56.688
They say witches used to seek it out.

00:14:56.771 --> 00:14:58.690
Witches?

00:15:01.735 --> 00:15:04.571
(wind blowing)

00:15:10.493 --> 00:15:13.288
(crackling, zapping)

00:15:21.546 --> 00:15:23.548
(crackling)

00:15:24.007 --> 00:15:26.009
(Tib and Gib meow)

00:15:40.565 --> 00:15:42.901
-(banging)
-Hmm?

00:15:43.735 --> 00:15:45.153
What's that?

00:15:51.117 --> 00:15:55.747
-(growling)
-Tib?

00:15:55.872 --> 00:15:57.332
What's the matter?

00:15:58.708 --> 00:16:00.001
What happened?

00:16:01.211 --> 00:16:03.213
(yowling)

00:16:03.672 --> 00:16:06.257
Did you get in some
sort of fight with Gib?

00:16:06.341 --> 00:16:09.219
-(yowling)
-Oh, you're shivering.

00:16:12.389 --> 00:16:15.475
Don't be scared now, I've got you.

00:16:17.894 --> 00:16:21.147
Let's get some rest
and tomorrow we'll go look for Gib.

00:16:39.624 --> 00:16:40.917
Tib?

00:16:43.545 --> 00:16:44.921
Where's he gone?

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:48.383
I wonder if he went to go look
for Gib by himself?

00:16:48.967 --> 00:16:50.927
Charlotte:
Mary.

00:16:51.928 --> 00:16:54.556
-Good morning, Great Aunt Charlotte.
-Good morning, dear.

00:16:54.681 --> 00:16:56.933
Mary, I have a little favor to ask of you.

00:16:57.016 --> 00:16:59.102
If you wouldn't mind.

00:16:59.227 --> 00:17:02.313
A favor, no, not at all.

00:17:03.815 --> 00:17:06.985
Would you deliver this for me?

00:17:07.068 --> 00:17:08.361
Of course I will.

00:17:08.486 --> 00:17:11.823
Charlotte: Here, I've written down
the name and address for you.

00:17:13.408 --> 00:17:15.660
Right, consider it done.

00:17:15.702 --> 00:17:18.538
Oh, Mary, one more thing.
Don't go into the woods today.

00:17:18.663 --> 00:17:22.250
-There's a dreadful mist.
-Mary: Okay, bye!

00:17:23.501 --> 00:17:25.587
And off she goes (chuckles).

00:17:26.463 --> 00:17:28.590
(humming)

00:17:31.468 --> 00:17:34.679
"51 Village of Redmanor, to Peter."

00:17:36.598 --> 00:17:37.682
Peter?

00:17:40.727 --> 00:17:43.730
Of all the people in the village,
it has to be him.

00:17:45.607 --> 00:17:47.609
-Oh.
-Huh?

00:17:50.737 --> 00:17:53.114
Well, red-haired monkey.

00:17:54.532 --> 00:17:58.161
I happen to have a name, you know,
it's Mary Smith actually.

00:17:59.537 --> 00:18:01.539
Okay, hello, Mary.

00:18:04.751 --> 00:18:05.835
What's this?

00:18:05.877 --> 00:18:08.213
I don't know, something for you
from my Great Aunt Charlotte.

00:18:09.255 --> 00:18:12.300
Wow, raspberry jam!

00:18:12.425 --> 00:18:16.429
The raspberries from Redmanor
are the best ever! Yes!

00:18:16.513 --> 00:18:18.640
(laughing)

00:18:18.765 --> 00:18:22.060
Well, I'd better go say thank you.

00:18:22.143 --> 00:18:23.603
(clears throat)

00:18:23.728 --> 00:18:26.189
I can't chat now,
I'm going to go look for Tib.

00:18:26.231 --> 00:18:28.149
Tib? Oh!

00:18:29.901 --> 00:18:33.947
Wait. Mary, was Tib over
at your place last night?

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:37.242
-Yes, but he disappeared this morning.
-Was Gib there too?

00:18:37.367 --> 00:18:39.452
I haven't seen her since yesterday.

00:18:40.411 --> 00:18:45.458
She and Tib, I saw them
together in the woods yesterday.

00:18:45.542 --> 00:18:47.544
♪ ♪

00:18:48.837 --> 00:18:51.381
Peter: You really ought to stay away
from the woods.

00:18:51.506 --> 00:18:54.092
With all this mist, it's dangerous.

00:18:54.175 --> 00:18:56.219
You don't have to come along.

00:18:56.302 --> 00:18:57.971
I want to find him too.

00:18:58.054 --> 00:18:59.639
They are my cats, you know.

00:18:59.764 --> 00:19:01.683
Hey, stop!

00:19:01.766 --> 00:19:03.518
Everyone knows we're not
supposed to go into the woods

00:19:03.601 --> 00:19:05.061
on misty days!

00:19:06.938 --> 00:19:09.065
Eh, you're scared?

00:19:09.148 --> 00:19:11.359
-Coward.
-(gasps)

00:19:13.111 --> 00:19:15.613
Hey! I said wait, red-haired monkey!

00:19:15.697 --> 00:19:16.698
(gasps)

00:19:18.283 --> 00:19:19.868
You be quiet!

00:19:19.951 --> 00:19:22.954
It's not like I chose to have
this frizzy red hair!

00:19:23.079 --> 00:19:26.457
I hate it. I wish I could change,
but I can't!

00:19:26.541 --> 00:19:27.959
(gasps)

00:19:29.252 --> 00:19:30.378
Mary...

00:19:31.796 --> 00:19:33.506
Leave me alone!

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:38.219
-Hey, at least let me come with you.
-Don't you dare follow me.

00:19:38.344 --> 00:19:40.263
Fine, go by yourself.

00:19:44.392 --> 00:19:48.313
I will never, ever forgive him.
Never, ever, ever!

00:19:51.149 --> 00:19:53.151
♪ ♪

00:19:59.282 --> 00:20:00.992
It is misty.

00:20:03.286 --> 00:20:04.287
Tib!

00:20:06.205 --> 00:20:08.625
I thought I might find you here. Hmm?

00:20:08.708 --> 00:20:11.669
Tib, what are you doing with that flower?

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:18.927
Huh?

00:21:01.052 --> 00:21:02.178
(yelps)

00:21:04.222 --> 00:21:05.682
Oh!

00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:07.642
Ow.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:15.274
This isn't the way we came before.

00:21:19.696 --> 00:21:20.738
Tib!

00:21:23.282 --> 00:21:24.450
(gasps)

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:30.581
What's the matter, why did you bring me
all the way out here?

00:21:30.665 --> 00:21:31.791
Hmm?

00:21:35.253 --> 00:21:37.755
Is that a broomstick?

00:21:37.839 --> 00:21:41.801
It is. I wonder what it's doing
all the way out here.

00:21:42.802 --> 00:21:44.512
(grunts)

00:21:44.595 --> 00:21:46.597
(yelps)

00:21:48.141 --> 00:21:50.393
Wow, it must be really old.

00:21:50.476 --> 00:21:51.477
Hmm?

00:21:52.603 --> 00:21:56.024
I wonder what this says.

00:21:56.941 --> 00:22:00.570
But look at this, Tib.
It's exactly the right height for me.

00:22:00.653 --> 00:22:03.281
Maybe now I'll be able to help Zebedee.

00:22:07.035 --> 00:22:09.037
Oh... Wait.

00:22:12.206 --> 00:22:14.208
(Mary groans)

00:22:18.463 --> 00:22:20.631
Tib, what'd you do that for?

00:22:20.757 --> 00:22:22.216
(gasps)

00:22:30.767 --> 00:22:34.395
What is going on? (gasps)

00:22:38.524 --> 00:22:40.443
What did that flower do?

00:22:45.031 --> 00:22:48.242
Wait, hold on. (yelps)

00:22:56.876 --> 00:22:58.878
(panting)

00:23:02.048 --> 00:23:03.633
No!

00:23:07.261 --> 00:23:08.805
Please, put me down.

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:11.265
-(meows)
-(gasps)

00:23:13.476 --> 00:23:15.394
(Mary screaming)

00:23:15.478 --> 00:23:17.438
Eee!

00:23:25.947 --> 00:23:27.949
♪ ♪

00:23:30.159 --> 00:23:33.538
(yelling)

00:23:33.621 --> 00:23:36.415
No, no, no, no, no, no!

00:23:57.103 --> 00:23:58.104
Huh?

00:24:02.817 --> 00:24:05.611
Tib, where are we?

00:24:07.864 --> 00:24:10.116
-(meows)
-Hmm?

00:24:10.199 --> 00:24:11.450
(gasps)

00:24:11.534 --> 00:24:14.620
(thunder clapping)

00:24:15.454 --> 00:24:18.207
Where on earth are you taking me?

00:24:18.291 --> 00:24:22.295
(screaming)

00:24:44.817 --> 00:24:47.445
♪ ♪

00:24:55.494 --> 00:24:58.539
Tib, is this some sort of dream?

00:24:59.749 --> 00:25:00.958
(gasps)

00:25:16.224 --> 00:25:18.476
I wonder what's in there.

00:25:25.233 --> 00:25:26.859
What? Wait!

00:25:26.943 --> 00:25:28.694
What are you doing, stop!

00:25:28.819 --> 00:25:31.530
(screaming)

00:25:38.371 --> 00:25:39.914
Ow.

00:25:39.997 --> 00:25:42.458
-What did you do that for?
-(meows)

00:25:42.541 --> 00:25:43.668
Huh?

00:25:47.046 --> 00:25:49.465
Somebody really likes broomsticks.

00:25:49.548 --> 00:25:53.469
Flanagan: Well, now you've made
quite a mess, haven't you?

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:54.720
(Mary shrieks)

00:25:54.804 --> 00:25:57.181
I'm Flanagan,
and I get to clean all this up.

00:25:57.306 --> 00:26:01.102
So, guess you'll be wanting
a few lessons then.

00:26:01.185 --> 00:26:04.438
You attempted that landing
much too quickly.

00:26:04.522 --> 00:26:06.983
Whoa! Steady boy, steady there.

00:26:09.277 --> 00:26:13.864
Good lad, there's a good lad.
Well, that tickles!

00:26:13.990 --> 00:26:18.619
Now, you stand quiet, rest here
till you're needed again.

00:26:21.163 --> 00:26:22.915
Good broomstick.

00:26:22.999 --> 00:26:26.210
Now, make sure you take better
care of him from now on!

00:26:26.335 --> 00:26:29.297
All broomsticks should be parked
right here in the stables.

00:26:29.422 --> 00:26:31.590
That's a very strict rule here.

00:26:31.674 --> 00:26:35.428
But I don't even know where here is.
I've never even been here before.

00:26:35.511 --> 00:26:39.557
That's for sure, if I'd taught you, you'd
know how to ride that broomstick properly

00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:43.060
and not have fallen off at my feet,
making a great big mess.

00:26:43.144 --> 00:26:45.354
Wait. Did you say
you teach broomstick riding?

00:26:45.438 --> 00:26:47.231
I used to, but things change.

00:26:47.315 --> 00:26:49.525
The new students don't know
what they're missing.

00:26:49.608 --> 00:26:52.028
New students?
What do you mean?

00:26:52.111 --> 00:26:55.448
(laughing)

00:26:55.531 --> 00:26:57.533
As if you don't know what I mean.

00:26:57.616 --> 00:27:01.162
It's as plain as the nose on your familiar
that you're a new student.

00:27:01.245 --> 00:27:04.206
My familiar? No, his name's Tib, he's--

00:27:04.332 --> 00:27:06.667
(bell droning)

00:27:06.751 --> 00:27:09.462
Ho! Quick as you like!
That's the first bell.

00:27:09.545 --> 00:27:12.923
They're especially strict about tardiness!

00:27:12.965 --> 00:27:15.217
Hold on, wait up!

00:27:15.301 --> 00:27:19.347
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho. Oh. Hmm?

00:27:19.472 --> 00:27:21.432
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho...

00:27:21.515 --> 00:27:23.726
(Mary panting)

00:27:23.809 --> 00:27:25.561
What a terrible dream.

00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:31.192
-And why'd he call Tib a familiar?
-Mm. Because that's what he is.

00:27:31.275 --> 00:27:35.154
Black as night and eyes like emerald.
What else could he be?

00:27:35.279 --> 00:27:37.239
He's as much a familiar as you are a witch

00:27:37.323 --> 00:27:39.784
and that's as plain as
the nose on your wee face.

00:27:39.867 --> 00:27:40.701
No.

00:27:40.826 --> 00:27:42.453
Flanagan: You don't have
to pretend around here.

00:27:42.536 --> 00:27:45.539
Come now, let's not be late for classes
on your first day!

00:27:45.623 --> 00:27:49.251
But-but I'm not a new pupil.

00:27:50.086 --> 00:27:52.380
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho...

00:27:52.463 --> 00:27:54.090
And here we are.

00:27:54.173 --> 00:27:57.676
Mary: I didn't know you could get
so out of breath in a dream.

00:28:01.013 --> 00:28:04.392
-(yowling)
-Tib!

00:28:04.475 --> 00:28:09.855
Sorry. This little fellow will have to be
on a leash on campus, that's the rule.

00:28:09.939 --> 00:28:11.690
Campus?

00:28:13.609 --> 00:28:15.861
Of course, Endor College.

00:28:18.072 --> 00:28:19.865
Endor College.

00:28:20.616 --> 00:28:22.493
Flanagan:
This here's the main entrance.

00:28:22.576 --> 00:28:25.037
Many fine witches have
passed through these gates.

00:28:25.121 --> 00:28:28.040
As you know, it's one of
the most prestigious schools

00:28:28.124 --> 00:28:32.503
for witches, dating back
to the days of dragons.

00:28:34.422 --> 00:28:38.717
-I have to read something to you.
-Okay.

00:28:38.801 --> 00:28:41.720
This is Endor College
campus rule number one.

00:28:41.804 --> 00:28:44.682
Now learn this or there will be trouble.

00:28:44.807 --> 00:28:46.308
Trouble?

00:28:47.017 --> 00:28:47.893
Ready?

00:28:49.687 --> 00:28:54.150
"Trespassers will be transformed."
And repeat.

00:28:54.567 --> 00:28:57.361
"Trespassers will be transformed."

00:28:59.321 --> 00:29:02.116
That's right,
those who enter the campus falsely

00:29:02.199 --> 00:29:05.661
will be transformed into something
other than themselves.

00:29:06.912 --> 00:29:09.039
(banging)

00:29:13.544 --> 00:29:17.173
See you later! New pupils get the tour
from the headmistress herself.

00:29:17.256 --> 00:29:18.382
No, wait.

00:29:18.466 --> 00:29:22.261
Flanagan: Must be off!
Toodle-pip, bye now!

00:29:25.890 --> 00:29:27.266
What do you think, Tib?

00:29:36.567 --> 00:29:38.068
Should we go in?

00:30:06.096 --> 00:30:07.389
How peculiar?

00:30:07.515 --> 00:30:09.683
(banging)

00:30:12.770 --> 00:30:15.105
(Tib growls)

00:30:17.900 --> 00:30:19.735
Well, Tib, on we go.

00:30:19.860 --> 00:30:22.613
There's no sense in looking back.

00:30:32.831 --> 00:30:35.584
Don't be scared, Tib, I'm not scared.

00:30:35.668 --> 00:30:37.211
(grunting)

00:30:37.294 --> 00:30:39.296
(squeaking)

00:30:39.380 --> 00:30:41.549
(yelping)

00:30:46.262 --> 00:30:49.265
(whooshing)

00:30:59.233 --> 00:31:03.946
Welcome to you and your familiar.
You must be a new pupil.

00:31:04.655 --> 00:31:06.865
I think there may have been
some misunderstanding.

00:31:06.949 --> 00:31:08.450
(chuckles)

00:31:11.912 --> 00:31:15.165
With this lovely hair, I doubt it.

00:31:15.249 --> 00:31:17.167
I shouldn't be here.

00:31:17.251 --> 00:31:20.129
I hope you're not suggesting
you're some sort of trespasser.

00:31:20.212 --> 00:31:21.880
(shuddering)

00:31:22.006 --> 00:31:25.384
Me, no, I'm the new girl, that's me.

00:31:25.467 --> 00:31:28.053
Of course, excellent.

00:31:41.025 --> 00:31:43.027
(steam whistles)

00:31:56.540 --> 00:32:00.836
I am Headmistress Mumblechook.
And your name?

00:32:00.961 --> 00:32:03.714
Um, Mary Smith, madam.

00:32:03.797 --> 00:32:07.051
Welcome to Endor College, Mary Smith.

00:32:08.385 --> 00:32:09.219
Thanks.

00:32:12.723 --> 00:32:15.517
Hmm. You'll be pleased to know
that this is the most

00:32:15.601 --> 00:32:17.728
exceptionally exclusive college of magic.

00:32:17.811 --> 00:32:20.022
Only the chosen may enroll.

00:32:20.939 --> 00:32:22.524
College of magic?

00:32:24.234 --> 00:32:29.156
Come now, let me assist and acquaint you
with our curious campus.

00:32:38.916 --> 00:32:41.126
Mumblechook:
This is the main hall.

00:32:41.210 --> 00:32:45.923
Here we collect sunlight to illuminate
the college in all hours, all weather.

00:32:46.048 --> 00:32:50.886
-Mary: It's beautiful.
-It is that as well.

00:32:53.847 --> 00:32:57.142
-Student: It’s Madam Mumblechook.
-Look, Tib, over there.

00:32:57.226 --> 00:32:59.812
-Student: Morning, Madam.
-Mumblechook: Marvelous morning.

00:33:01.355 --> 00:33:05.234
-How do those elevators work?
-They're electric, my dear.

00:33:05.359 --> 00:33:08.362
Electricity is also a form of magic.

00:33:09.530 --> 00:33:11.073
Huh?

00:33:12.700 --> 00:33:14.702
What? What?

00:33:18.622 --> 00:33:22.543
Come and see the classrooms
and then we can discuss enrollment.

00:33:22.626 --> 00:33:23.794
(Mary gasps)

00:33:28.716 --> 00:33:30.884
(cloud whirring)

00:33:35.055 --> 00:33:37.307
This is the first-year classroom.

00:33:38.809 --> 00:33:42.187
As you can see, all first-years
have broomstick riding lessons.

00:33:42.271 --> 00:33:45.691
-And up straight.
-Mumblechook: It can take up to a year

00:33:45.816 --> 00:33:47.818
to master it completely.

00:33:47.860 --> 00:33:49.570
Mary:
I see.

00:33:49.653 --> 00:33:52.364
But you wouldn't need
anywhere near a year.

00:33:52.448 --> 00:33:53.490
Why?

00:33:53.574 --> 00:33:56.869
I saw you arrive, you were
quite adept with that broomstick.

00:33:56.952 --> 00:33:58.620
(laughs)

00:33:58.704 --> 00:34:01.665
Now, let's have you see something
a little more specialized.

00:34:01.749 --> 00:34:03.292
Specialized?

00:34:03.417 --> 00:34:06.920
Magic aeronautics,
magic history, magic chemistry.

00:34:07.004 --> 00:34:10.174
We offer a multitude
of magical majors here.

00:34:10.299 --> 00:34:12.426
But at Endor College,
what we are best known for

00:34:12.509 --> 00:34:15.637
are our courses on transformation.

00:34:15.721 --> 00:34:18.182
Decidedly the most difficult.

00:34:18.265 --> 00:34:20.017
I'm sure.

00:34:20.142 --> 00:34:22.144
Oh, dear.

00:34:24.313 --> 00:34:27.316
Seems like there'll be
an awful lot of studying.

00:34:27.399 --> 00:34:30.736
What about sports or field trips even?

00:34:30.819 --> 00:34:33.947
Certainly, there are
many recreations here.

00:34:35.574 --> 00:34:41.872
My personal favorite is
the aerial gymkhana, held in December.

00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:46.543
We cultivate witches and warlocks
who excel in mind, body and spirit.

00:34:49.046 --> 00:34:50.756
Amazing.

00:34:50.839 --> 00:34:54.134
Mumblechook:
The dining hall is state of the art.

00:34:54.218 --> 00:34:57.346
Students eat whatever they please.
Every meal is nutritionally balanced

00:34:57.429 --> 00:34:59.890
and mouth wateringly delicious.

00:34:59.973 --> 00:35:03.435
I think my favorite subject will be lunch.

00:35:04.269 --> 00:35:09.358
Mary, someone with your talent
would certainly be a credit to Endor.

00:35:09.441 --> 00:35:13.445
-Quite extraordinary.
-Mary: Talent, talent for what?

00:35:13.529 --> 00:35:17.032
As a witch, Mary Smith,
a remarkable witch.

00:35:17.115 --> 00:35:20.202
Do you really think I didn't see
the insignia on your hand?

00:35:20.285 --> 00:35:22.871
Mary:
What? Oh, this.

00:35:22.955 --> 00:35:27.835
Yes, that. And no schooling,
and yet look how much you can do.

00:35:27.918 --> 00:35:30.295
Witches your age can barely sweep up
with a broomstick,

00:35:30.379 --> 00:35:33.048
let alone, ride one.
And you've somehow tamed

00:35:33.131 --> 00:35:34.925
a perfect familiar.

00:35:35.050 --> 00:35:38.762
Thanks, I'm not used to compliments.
I'm blushing I think.

00:35:38.846 --> 00:35:41.431
My dear, have a look and see.

00:35:45.310 --> 00:35:49.481
This red hair of yours,
like a burning flame.

00:35:49.565 --> 00:35:53.652
Red-haired witches have always
been supremely superior.

00:35:53.735 --> 00:35:58.574
No other color is more coveted
for witches, and on someone like you.

00:36:00.367 --> 00:36:03.203
You're a once-in-a-century talent.

00:36:06.039 --> 00:36:07.499
(Mary giggles)

00:36:11.879 --> 00:36:14.339
Mumblechook:
This is the laboratory.

00:36:14.423 --> 00:36:16.425
In the second year,
you'll immerse yourself

00:36:16.508 --> 00:36:18.677
in the study of chemistry.

00:36:18.802 --> 00:36:20.971
Mary:
Chemistry, not magic?

00:36:21.054 --> 00:36:24.141
What is potion making
but chemistry by another name?

00:36:24.224 --> 00:36:27.352
As the renowned Dr. Dee is fond of saying.

00:36:27.436 --> 00:36:31.398
-Surely, you've heard of him?
-What, what, yes, of course I have.

00:36:31.523 --> 00:36:33.942
Um, Dr. Dee (chuckles).

00:36:34.776 --> 00:36:37.404
Mm. I'd like you to meet him.

00:36:37.487 --> 00:36:39.823
Doctor! Dr. Dee!

00:36:39.907 --> 00:36:43.577
Madam Mumblechook,
you know I hate induction--

00:36:43.660 --> 00:36:46.455
I mean interruptions.

00:36:46.538 --> 00:36:48.999
I am conducting an analysis
of the test results

00:36:49.082 --> 00:36:51.335
we collected the other day.

00:36:51.418 --> 00:36:53.670
I must calibrate every
comparative compound

00:36:53.754 --> 00:36:56.423
with absolute zero interference.

00:36:56.506 --> 00:36:59.968
My positive energy is being
used to devise meticulous plans.

00:37:01.595 --> 00:37:05.265
Doctor, allow me to introduce
our newest pupil, Miss Mary Smith.

00:37:05.349 --> 00:37:09.686
She is a genuine prodigy,
and look at this ravishing red hair.

00:37:09.770 --> 00:37:13.440
Indeed, red, ruby,
crimson, scarlet, copper,

00:37:13.523 --> 00:37:15.651
all marvelous colors, marvelous, yes.

00:37:15.734 --> 00:37:19.821
The recessive gene that causes red hair
only occurs in 1% to 2% of the population,

00:37:19.905 --> 00:37:23.450
but I'm forgetting my manners.
How do you do, Miss Mary?

00:37:23.533 --> 00:37:25.661
Mary:
How do you do?

00:37:25.744 --> 00:37:27.955
Dr. Dee does well,
and what he doesn't know

00:37:28.038 --> 00:37:30.165
about science and magic, he soon will.

00:37:30.248 --> 00:37:32.626
I have a question for you, Mary.

00:37:32.709 --> 00:37:34.419
Now, if we have two virtual worlds

00:37:34.503 --> 00:37:37.255
in two different dimensions
and call the one on the plane

00:37:37.339 --> 00:37:39.925
of X "Pattern Turtle,"
and we call the dimension

00:37:40.008 --> 00:37:42.344
that represents magic "Pattern Crane,"

00:37:42.427 --> 00:37:45.347
which of the two patterns do you think
is the more effective approach

00:37:45.430 --> 00:37:50.727
in biogeochemical analysis?
Hmm? Any ideas?

00:37:50.811 --> 00:37:53.855
-Uh...
-Pattern turtle or pattern crane?

00:37:53.939 --> 00:37:55.440
Turtle, I think.

00:37:55.524 --> 00:37:58.610
Turtle, you say, that's impossible!

00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:04.408
No, you're right, you may indeed be right!

00:38:04.533 --> 00:38:06.451
You've carved out a new path!

00:38:06.535 --> 00:38:08.495
Splendid, Mary, splendid!

00:38:08.578 --> 00:38:12.249
So you're well versed in chemistry.

00:38:12.374 --> 00:38:15.544
Yeah, I'm not bad at science.

00:38:15.627 --> 00:38:20.007
Dr. Dee: Excellent! Then shall I show you
my most advanced class?

00:38:20.090 --> 00:38:21.758
Mary:
Yes, please.

00:38:24.970 --> 00:38:26.972
(elevator dings)

00:38:30.642 --> 00:38:33.979
These are the finest students
at Endor College.

00:38:34.104 --> 00:38:35.147
What?

00:38:37.024 --> 00:38:38.108
Where?

00:38:40.527 --> 00:38:42.112
I don't see anyone.

00:38:43.905 --> 00:38:47.200
Exactly, it's going rather well.

00:38:47.284 --> 00:38:49.536
-(claps)
-Huh?

00:38:56.001 --> 00:38:58.003
(Mary gasping)

00:39:00.881 --> 00:39:01.923
Oh my.

00:39:03.842 --> 00:39:06.762
Invisibility is
the most difficult discipline.

00:39:06.887 --> 00:39:08.597
Let's see you try it.

00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:09.890
-Grizel!
-What?

00:39:09.931 --> 00:39:12.684
Dr. Dee:
Let her borrow your orb.

00:39:12.768 --> 00:39:17.105
Mary: That's okay, I'm not really
interested in invisibility.

00:39:17.189 --> 00:39:19.858
-Here!
-(gasps)

00:39:21.193 --> 00:39:23.612
(Tib growls)

00:39:23.695 --> 00:39:24.654
Sorry, Tib.

00:39:24.738 --> 00:39:27.282
Now watch the orb
and concentrate, my dear.

00:39:27.365 --> 00:39:28.366
But...

00:39:31.078 --> 00:39:32.746
The fly-by-night marks.

00:39:32.829 --> 00:39:38.210
Now, Miss Mary, dissolve every cell,
every atom in your body.

00:39:38.293 --> 00:39:42.672
Concentrate on the fusion
between magic and mind.

00:39:42.756 --> 00:39:45.008
-(applauding)
-(Tib meows)

00:39:45.092 --> 00:39:47.094
Huh?

00:39:47.886 --> 00:39:50.305
Fine. Whatever happens, happens.

00:39:51.348 --> 00:39:53.350
Now what did Dr. Dee say?

00:39:53.433 --> 00:39:56.436
Dissolve my cells, disappear, disappear,

00:39:56.520 --> 00:40:00.273
disappear, disappear, disappear,

00:40:00.398 --> 00:40:04.111
disappear, disappear,
disappear, disappear...

00:40:04.194 --> 00:40:07.155
-She's doing it.
-Superb!

00:40:07.239 --> 00:40:11.201
-(meows)
-Disappear, disappear, disappear,

00:40:11.284 --> 00:40:14.162
-disappear, disappear, disappear!
-(Tib yowling)

00:40:14.246 --> 00:40:16.748
Now what? What's happening?

00:40:24.798 --> 00:40:28.510
Could it be that she's
actually surpassed the ability

00:40:28.593 --> 00:40:30.762
to make herself invisible?

00:40:34.391 --> 00:40:36.518
This is not going well.

00:40:36.601 --> 00:40:38.979
(Tib yowls)

00:40:40.355 --> 00:40:41.189
Tib!

00:41:00.083 --> 00:41:04.963
Excellent! That was
quite excellent, Mary Smith.

00:41:05.046 --> 00:41:09.718
Where did you acquire such skill?
For that was most advanced.

00:41:09.801 --> 00:41:11.469
Well, I didn't expect that.

00:41:11.553 --> 00:41:16.057
You may well be a prodigy the likes
of which are rarely seen, Miss Mary.

00:41:16.141 --> 00:41:17.684
Me? No.

00:41:17.767 --> 00:41:21.062
That is the power of the red-haired witch.

00:41:21.146 --> 00:41:25.650
-(students chattering)
-She's amazing.

00:41:26.860 --> 00:41:31.489
Yes, I mean that was
probably only 40% of my power.

00:41:31.573 --> 00:41:33.408
(students chattering loudly)

00:41:33.491 --> 00:41:34.993
Dr. Dee:
Extraordinary.

00:41:35.076 --> 00:41:37.787
What an honor it is
to welcome such a witch.

00:41:37.871 --> 00:41:39.289
Whilst clearly you will learn from us,

00:41:39.372 --> 00:41:42.209
it seems we may ultimately
learn something from you.

00:41:42.292 --> 00:41:43.835
Welcome, dear.

00:41:44.920 --> 00:41:47.339
Thank you, I'm looking
forward to it, Madam.

00:41:47.422 --> 00:41:51.426
A round of applause for the enrollment
of Mary Smith, a prodigy who has reached

00:41:51.509 --> 00:41:54.930
the convergent of boundary between
magical ability and scientific mind!

00:41:55.013 --> 00:41:57.849
(cheering)

00:41:57.933 --> 00:42:01.561
We'll be fine, Tib. I'll make
a great witch, you'll see.

00:42:04.189 --> 00:42:06.691
(ringing)

00:42:06.775 --> 00:42:08.860
Mary:
What a day, eh, Tib?

00:42:08.944 --> 00:42:11.196
When we get to my office,
I'll give you the enrollment

00:42:11.279 --> 00:42:14.866
-forms to fill out straight away.
-Mary: Yes, with pleasure.

00:42:24.209 --> 00:42:29.381
This is where I carry out my experiments
in transformation magic.

00:42:30.382 --> 00:42:32.384
Mary:
Transformation magic?

00:42:34.552 --> 00:42:36.846
It's a strongroom, we need to make sure

00:42:36.972 --> 00:42:40.850
that the transformation
experiments are secure.

00:42:44.104 --> 00:42:45.063
(gasps)

00:42:46.523 --> 00:42:51.152
Hmm. This one should make
an excellent test subject.

00:42:51.236 --> 00:42:54.197
(monkey screeching)

00:42:54.281 --> 00:42:56.283
Mumblechook:
Oh, Dr. Dee has had wonderful success

00:42:56.366 --> 00:43:01.871
turning powerless animals
into magical beings.

00:43:01.955 --> 00:43:04.291
Mary:
Powerless animals?

00:43:11.464 --> 00:43:13.258
(Tib screeches)

00:43:13.341 --> 00:43:15.093
Tib!

00:43:16.428 --> 00:43:17.262
No, no.

00:43:20.390 --> 00:43:23.727
(Tib screehes, yowls)

00:43:23.810 --> 00:43:25.645
Tib, what's wrong with you?

00:43:25.729 --> 00:43:29.316
(laughs) You ought to keep better control
of your familiar.

00:43:29.399 --> 00:43:32.986
-Sorry.
-(roaring)

00:43:34.237 --> 00:43:36.573
-(gasps)
-Hmm.

00:43:37.073 --> 00:43:39.200
Dr. Dee, what was that?

00:43:39.284 --> 00:43:43.121
Failures. Alas, there can be
no progress without failures.

00:43:43.204 --> 00:43:44.706
Failures?

00:43:44.789 --> 00:43:48.376
Oh yes, each one a lesson!

00:43:48.460 --> 00:43:51.046
The building blocks of success.

00:43:52.922 --> 00:43:57.302
You see, the development of science
and magic is built on failures.

00:43:57.385 --> 00:43:59.220
See you in one diurnal turning,
little prodigy.

00:44:05.894 --> 00:44:08.855
Mumblechook: Come along, Miss Mary.
You should be on your way

00:44:08.938 --> 00:44:11.733
before it gets dark.

00:44:11.816 --> 00:44:13.193
Coming.

00:44:20.617 --> 00:44:23.078
Mumblechook:
♪ Enrollment forms, enrollment forms ♪

00:44:23.161 --> 00:44:26.081
♪ Where did I put
those enrollment forms? ♪

00:44:26.164 --> 00:44:29.417
I'm sorry, do feel free
to wait for me upstairs.

00:44:29.501 --> 00:44:31.086
Oh sure.

00:44:34.672 --> 00:44:37.759
It must be here somewhere.

00:44:38.426 --> 00:44:42.514
You'll find some interesting
artifacts up there.

00:44:42.597 --> 00:44:45.433
It's my personal museum of magic.

00:44:45.517 --> 00:44:48.395
I'm very proud of it.

00:44:48.478 --> 00:44:52.565
Some of the items date
back to ancient times.

00:44:55.068 --> 00:44:56.820
Oh my.

00:45:00.698 --> 00:45:02.242
(gasps)

00:45:02.325 --> 00:45:04.369
Mumblechook:
Well, how odd.

00:45:04.452 --> 00:45:08.498
The application form for all new students
should be here somewhere.

00:45:15.213 --> 00:45:16.464
Fly-by-night.

00:45:19.467 --> 00:45:21.636
(gasps)

00:45:40.363 --> 00:45:42.365
-(Mary's voice): Master Spells.
-Eh?

00:45:43.825 --> 00:45:47.454
The spell to eliminate darkness.
The spell to make something rotten.

00:45:47.537 --> 00:45:51.958
The spell to ease stomach pain.
The spell to deflect an enemy's attack.

00:45:52.041 --> 00:45:54.961
A book of magic spells.

00:45:55.044 --> 00:45:57.130
Mumblechook: Mary, my dear,
perhaps you should serve

00:45:57.213 --> 00:45:59.841
as the Endor College
student representative?

00:45:59.924 --> 00:46:01.759
You could start tomorrow.

00:46:01.843 --> 00:46:04.512
What? Really?

00:46:04.596 --> 00:46:07.640
Yes, really, you're more than qualified.

00:46:07.724 --> 00:46:09.809
I can't think of anyone better
to represent the school.

00:46:09.893 --> 00:46:15.398
Let's see, perhaps you should also head up
the Festival Committee.

00:46:15.482 --> 00:46:19.360
-Maybe.
-And you could lead the study tours.

00:46:19.444 --> 00:46:21.488
Wouldn't it be wonderful
if you could represent us

00:46:21.571 --> 00:46:23.740
at the academic conference too?

00:46:23.823 --> 00:46:25.283
Well, some people might
get a little bit jealous,

00:46:25.366 --> 00:46:28.495
but no starting student has
ever been this talented.

00:46:28.578 --> 00:46:33.208
-Madam, wait, I'm not.
-Mumblechook: Not what?

00:46:33.291 --> 00:46:37.128
It's not true, I'm not talented.

00:46:37.212 --> 00:46:41.758
I can fly on a broomstick
and I can become invisible,

00:46:41.841 --> 00:46:45.053
but it's all thanks
to a mysterious flower.

00:46:48.556 --> 00:46:49.724
Flower?

00:46:52.810 --> 00:46:55.104
Did you say a flower?

00:46:55.188 --> 00:46:58.900
-Mary: Well--
-A mysterious flower, Mary?

00:46:58.983 --> 00:47:01.486
-Yes, but I--
-Where is it?

00:47:01.569 --> 00:47:02.570
What?

00:47:02.654 --> 00:47:05.031
You appear to be hiding
something behind your back.

00:47:05.114 --> 00:47:08.409
Mary:
Me? No, no, no, no.

00:47:08.493 --> 00:47:10.328
Mumblechook
Then what is it that you're holding?

00:47:10.411 --> 00:47:13.498
Mary:
Oh no, it's nothing.

00:47:13.581 --> 00:47:16.000
-Show me your hands!
-(gasps)

00:47:19.754 --> 00:47:23.550
Oh, and what might this be, my dear?

00:47:26.553 --> 00:47:29.264
I don't recognize these strange symbols.

00:47:31.182 --> 00:47:36.729
"51 Village of Redmanor, to Peter." Hmm.

00:47:36.813 --> 00:47:39.649
Yes, you see the flower belongs to him.

00:47:39.732 --> 00:47:42.819
I don't really understand
how it works myself.

00:47:45.029 --> 00:47:48.157
Peter's very talented, much more than me.

00:47:48.241 --> 00:47:50.994
I'd like to keep this if I may, Mary?

00:47:51.077 --> 00:47:53.204
Uh... Sure.

00:47:53.288 --> 00:47:56.749
Tremendous, in that case I'll go and fetch
the enrollment form.

00:47:57.625 --> 00:48:01.671
You'll fill it out and
bring it tomorrow, all right?

00:48:01.754 --> 00:48:02.839
Yes, ma'am.

00:48:07.969 --> 00:48:13.016
No need to see me off,
I can find my own way.

00:48:13.099 --> 00:48:15.643
But thank you for today.

00:48:15.727 --> 00:48:19.522
And tomorrow, we'll debate
the discontinuity of Filio Functions.

00:48:19.606 --> 00:48:21.399
Look who's here.

00:48:25.486 --> 00:48:26.904
My broomstick!

00:48:29.365 --> 00:48:32.910
Well, now, your mistress
has come back for you.

00:48:36.748 --> 00:48:39.208
But I'm not sure I can
find my own way home.

00:48:39.292 --> 00:48:43.504
-Don't worry, the broom knows the way.
-Oh, that's good.

00:48:47.592 --> 00:48:51.638
Am I glad to see you.
Now, nice and gentle.

00:48:51.721 --> 00:48:53.389
Come on, Tib, we're off now.

00:48:54.557 --> 00:48:55.558
Tib?

00:48:56.684 --> 00:48:59.896
-What's the matter?
-He's a cat, so he might just be sulking,

00:48:59.979 --> 00:49:03.316
you never know with them, or perhaps,
he doesn't wanna leave.

00:49:03.399 --> 00:49:05.652
Cats do have an affinity
for magic after all.

00:49:10.823 --> 00:49:15.828
Tib, let's go home. I'll give you
a nice saucer of warm milk.

00:49:26.130 --> 00:49:29.300
-Good, now I want you to hold on tight.
-Okay.

00:49:29.384 --> 00:49:30.718
Hmm?

00:49:34.013 --> 00:49:36.015
The girl's broomstick.

00:49:37.892 --> 00:49:40.937
You've a good broomstick there,
look after it.

00:49:41.688 --> 00:49:44.691
-Away!
-(Mary screams)

00:49:46.526 --> 00:49:49.278
Mary:
I said gentle this time!

00:49:52.907 --> 00:49:55.827
Congratulations, madam,
what a splendid witch

00:49:55.910 --> 00:49:58.538
we have enrolling with us.

00:49:58.621 --> 00:50:01.708
That girl has discovered
where the flowers are.

00:50:01.791 --> 00:50:05.336
A discovery indeed--
What did you just say?

00:50:05.420 --> 00:50:08.589
-The flowers, you don't mean?
-Yes.

00:50:08.673 --> 00:50:13.344
The stolen fly-by-night? How could you
possibly let her leave, Madam?

00:50:15.263 --> 00:50:17.432
She's going to bring them right to us.

00:50:24.522 --> 00:50:26.983
We have her like a cat on a leash.

00:50:35.450 --> 00:50:38.870
Oh the book, I shouldn't have taken it.

00:50:40.538 --> 00:50:42.081
Tib, are you okay?

00:50:44.167 --> 00:50:45.877
Are you cross with me?

00:50:45.960 --> 00:50:49.297
I was scared, I didn't mean to take it.

00:50:49.380 --> 00:50:51.758
It just sort of happened.

00:50:51.841 --> 00:50:53.968
At least we got away
before madam realized.

00:50:54.051 --> 00:50:56.137
I thought she was going to eat me alive.

00:50:56.220 --> 00:50:59.140
Any one else would've done the same thing.

00:50:59.223 --> 00:51:01.559
(screaming)

00:51:24.123 --> 00:51:26.375
(groans)

00:51:32.882 --> 00:51:34.383
Little broomstick.

00:51:37.762 --> 00:51:42.517
I guess the magic's faded,
but it wasn't a dream, was it?

00:51:47.438 --> 00:51:49.607
Tib!

00:51:51.025 --> 00:51:54.779
He's gone.
He's so moody.

00:52:07.792 --> 00:52:09.877
(grunts)

00:52:12.463 --> 00:52:14.298
(whimpers)

00:52:14.382 --> 00:52:16.092
My bum.

00:52:16.801 --> 00:52:19.095
-(doors open)
-Mary?

00:52:22.306 --> 00:52:24.058
Is that you, Mary?

00:52:25.476 --> 00:52:27.895
Great Aunt Charlotte!

00:52:34.569 --> 00:52:36.404
I'm not dreaming, I knew it.

00:52:37.947 --> 00:52:41.200
We were very worried, you know, Mary.

00:52:49.959 --> 00:52:53.296
Mary, slow down, you'll get indigestion.

00:52:53.379 --> 00:52:55.756
Sorry, but I'm so hungry, Miss Banks.

00:52:55.840 --> 00:52:58.551
It must've been
a wonderful day then, Mary.

00:52:58.634 --> 00:53:01.012
Um, let me see, mm!

00:53:01.679 --> 00:53:04.307
Yes, it really was. It was very exciting.

00:53:04.390 --> 00:53:08.102
Do try to come home
a little earlier tomorrow, eh?

00:53:08.185 --> 00:53:10.354
Now Miss Banks, go easy on her.

00:53:10.438 --> 00:53:13.774
Mary's back safe and sound, right?

00:53:13.858 --> 00:53:17.028
Oh yes, and it's so nice to be home.

00:53:18.905 --> 00:53:23.284
-Home, you say?
-Mary: Mm-hmm!

00:53:28.039 --> 00:53:30.041
(sighs)

00:53:41.302 --> 00:53:43.304
"Fill out the enrollment form
and bring it tomorrow

00:53:43.387 --> 00:53:45.514
if you would be so kind, Miss Smith."

00:53:45.598 --> 00:53:48.059
(giggles) I am not going back there.

00:53:49.644 --> 00:53:53.856
"You truly are a remarkable
talent with your red hair.

00:53:53.940 --> 00:53:56.901
"You may well be a prodigy, Miss Mary.

00:53:56.984 --> 00:54:00.488
You should serve as Endor
student representative."

00:54:00.571 --> 00:54:02.740
(knocking on door)

00:54:04.325 --> 00:54:05.409
Hmm?

00:54:05.493 --> 00:54:07.036
(banging on door)

00:54:07.119 --> 00:54:10.039
Miss Banks:
I'm coming.

00:54:10.122 --> 00:54:11.582
(door opens)

00:54:11.666 --> 00:54:14.043
Zebedee, what is it?
What's the matter?

00:54:14.126 --> 00:54:16.420
Zebedee: It's Peter,
we can't find him anywhere.

00:54:16.504 --> 00:54:17.713
Peter?

00:54:18.297 --> 00:54:20.549
Charlotte: Zebedee,
what do you think has happened?

00:54:20.633 --> 00:54:23.844
No one's seen him,
he's been missing all afternoon.

00:54:23.928 --> 00:54:27.807
His bicycle was found
on the edge of the woods.

00:54:27.890 --> 00:54:31.811
Miss Banks: He's not gone into the woods
with all that mist about.

00:54:31.894 --> 00:54:33.396
Oh my goodness.

00:54:33.479 --> 00:54:35.398
Miss Banks: Now, now,
it's Peter we're talking about.

00:54:35.481 --> 00:54:37.191
He'll be home in no time.

00:54:37.274 --> 00:54:40.403
We're looking everywhere.
I'm sure we'll find him.

00:54:40.486 --> 00:54:42.029
Charlotte:
Do take care.

00:54:42.113 --> 00:54:44.240
Miss Banks:
Give our regards to his mother.

00:54:44.323 --> 00:54:46.075
I will, good night.

00:54:55.793 --> 00:54:58.462
He must've gone back into the woods
looking for me.

00:54:58.546 --> 00:55:03.009
-(banging)
-(Tib yowling)

00:55:04.552 --> 00:55:07.304
-(screeching)
-Tib!

00:55:23.487 --> 00:55:27.033
-(Tib screeches)
-What's this?

00:55:29.744 --> 00:55:32.580
Mary Smith, the impostor witch.

00:55:32.663 --> 00:55:38.085
How dare you taint the noble establishment
that is Endor College.

00:55:38.169 --> 00:55:42.631
Did you really think you could fool us?

00:55:42.715 --> 00:55:45.176
Well, now, it seems that
your friend has drifted here

00:55:45.259 --> 00:55:47.303
along with the mist.

00:55:48.471 --> 00:55:49.930
Mary:
Peter!

00:55:50.014 --> 00:55:54.685
Mumblechook: It was easy finding him,
thanks to all your help.

00:55:55.227 --> 00:56:00.357
If you want to save him, you must bring me
the witch's flower.

00:56:00.441 --> 00:56:02.860
And since it only blooms
once every seven years,

00:56:02.943 --> 00:56:07.656
you'd better be quick,
but if you decide not to come,

00:56:07.740 --> 00:56:09.533
there's a rule, remember?

00:56:09.617 --> 00:56:13.120
That all trespassers will be transformed.

00:56:16.040 --> 00:56:18.876
I'll see you soon, impostor witch.

00:56:20.628 --> 00:56:22.797
(Tib growls)

00:56:31.305 --> 00:56:32.807
(gasps)

00:56:35.976 --> 00:56:37.478
It's all my fault.

00:57:10.261 --> 00:57:12.346
(Tib meows)

00:57:13.973 --> 00:57:16.559
I know, Tib, but we have to go.

00:57:49.216 --> 00:57:50.718
Hey wait!

00:57:50.801 --> 00:57:55.723
(yelping)

00:58:04.481 --> 00:58:05.482
Mary?

00:58:08.903 --> 00:58:13.032
Please, I need you to fly
quietly or we'll be found out.

00:58:18.996 --> 00:58:20.039
Come on, Tib.

00:58:25.836 --> 00:58:27.630
To Endor College.

00:58:38.390 --> 00:58:40.726
Mary? Where are you?

00:58:59.036 --> 00:59:01.247
(gasps) But this is...

00:59:09.004 --> 00:59:12.007
(panting)

00:59:17.429 --> 00:59:18.639
Mary.

00:59:44.707 --> 00:59:45.708
Thank you.

00:59:48.294 --> 00:59:51.422
-Wait for me here.
-(broom mumbles)

01:00:05.644 --> 01:00:06.979
Here we go, Tib.

01:00:09.565 --> 01:00:11.400
Hey, hey, wait for me.

01:00:12.609 --> 01:00:15.279
♪ ♪

01:00:20.034 --> 01:00:25.247
Mumblechook:
Oh look who it is. Back so soon?

01:00:29.001 --> 01:00:33.255
Needless to say we've been expecting you.

01:00:33.339 --> 01:00:38.385
Indeed, in fact your return was faster
than Gelman's magical reaction.

01:00:42.598 --> 01:00:47.728
-Now, where is he?
-Excellent, the fly-by-night!

01:00:47.811 --> 01:00:51.857
It's quite dangerous,
much safer if you just hand it over.

01:00:51.940 --> 01:00:55.611
Where is Peter?
You said you'd let him go.

01:01:02.117 --> 01:01:03.786
Give that back, hey!

01:01:09.833 --> 01:01:11.752
Well done, thank you.

01:01:20.886 --> 01:01:23.138
(gasping)

01:01:23.222 --> 01:01:25.933
How long I've waited.

01:01:26.016 --> 01:01:29.853
Mary:
Get your creepy hands off me!

01:01:30.896 --> 01:01:33.148
Take her to the strongroom.

01:01:33.232 --> 01:01:37.319
I want to study her later,
so handle her with care.

01:01:37.403 --> 01:01:42.366
Liars! Cowards!
This isn't what we agreed to!

01:01:51.959 --> 01:01:53.961
(grunts)

01:01:54.044 --> 01:01:56.046
Ow.

01:01:56.130 --> 01:01:59.216
-(door clanking)
-Familiar: Bye-bye.

01:02:12.563 --> 01:02:15.023
Now what? Tib?

01:02:16.275 --> 01:02:17.401
Hmm?

01:02:19.486 --> 01:02:20.529
Tib?

01:02:25.242 --> 01:02:27.995
-(growling)
-Hmm?

01:02:29.955 --> 01:02:31.623
-(growls)
-Are you in there?

01:02:38.130 --> 01:02:40.382
(yelling)

01:02:42.509 --> 01:02:45.596
(creatures snarling)

01:02:53.187 --> 01:02:55.063
All these creatures.

01:02:57.441 --> 01:03:01.820
These must be the failures
that Dr. Dee was talking about.

01:03:01.904 --> 01:03:04.406
(roars)

01:03:04.490 --> 01:03:06.492
(growls)

01:03:06.575 --> 01:03:11.038
He used you poor animals for
his transformation experiments.

01:03:11.121 --> 01:03:14.208
-Awful.
-(Tib screeching)

01:03:14.291 --> 01:03:15.375
Tib!

01:03:18.921 --> 01:03:21.215
Tib, what have you found?

01:03:21.298 --> 01:03:23.258
(both vocalizing)

01:03:26.011 --> 01:03:28.514
Gib, is that you?

01:03:30.390 --> 01:03:34.228
Now I see, Tib, you brought me here
to help find your girlfriend.

01:03:34.311 --> 01:03:36.522
(vocalizing)

01:03:42.361 --> 01:03:45.030
Now if only we could find Peter.

01:03:45.113 --> 01:03:46.865
(running footsteps)

01:03:48.575 --> 01:03:50.285
(gasps)

01:03:50.369 --> 01:03:53.830
Peter:
You witch, get me out of here.

01:03:53.914 --> 01:03:55.832
Mary:
Peter!

01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:59.545
Mary, what are you doing here?

01:04:00.504 --> 01:04:03.215
(crying)

01:04:03.298 --> 01:04:04.550
Mary?

01:04:06.260 --> 01:04:09.179
You okay? Say something.

01:04:09.263 --> 01:04:11.098
I'm so sorry, Peter!

01:04:11.181 --> 01:04:14.101
(sobbing)

01:04:15.936 --> 01:04:17.563
That's all right.

01:04:18.605 --> 01:04:20.607
Dr. Dee:
This is it, without a doubt.

01:04:20.691 --> 01:04:25.529
We can once again resume the final phase
of our transformation experiment.

01:04:25.612 --> 01:04:28.615
All thanks to this little flower.

01:04:28.699 --> 01:04:30.325
♪ Tadpoles become frogs ♪

01:04:30.409 --> 01:04:32.202
♪ Caterpillars, butterflies ♪

01:04:32.286 --> 01:04:34.997
At long last, with this power,
the students of Endor

01:04:35.080 --> 01:04:39.710
will graduate as the most powerful witches
and warlocks ever known.

01:04:39.793 --> 01:04:42.713
Dr. Dee: And those witches and warlocks
will change the world.

01:04:42.796 --> 01:04:44.756
We've waited so long.

01:04:45.424 --> 01:04:50.679
We can put the previous tragedy behind us.
This time we will definitely succeed.

01:04:50.762 --> 01:04:53.473
And we're in possession
of a much younger subject this time,

01:04:53.557 --> 01:04:55.892
we can't go wrong.

01:04:56.643 --> 01:05:00.397
And let us not forget,
his inherent innocence.

01:05:00.480 --> 01:05:04.276
Yes, yes, yes, yes, of course.

01:05:04.359 --> 01:05:08.113
Innocence has a catalytic effect
on the absorption of magic.

01:05:08.196 --> 01:05:11.575
I shall prepare at once.
Familiars, to the laboratory.

01:05:15.537 --> 01:05:18.248
Mary:
I'm sorry.

01:05:18.332 --> 01:05:25.130
Peter: Poor Gib, I wish they could've
changed me instead into an adult.

01:05:25.881 --> 01:05:29.384
Just like that, sure to make
my mum's life easier.

01:05:29.468 --> 01:05:32.179
I could help out more and I could take
the burden off of her a bit.

01:05:33.764 --> 01:05:37.517
You're not the only one
who wishes they could change.

01:05:37.601 --> 01:05:38.518
Peter.

01:05:41.563 --> 01:05:45.525
We have to at least try
to get out of this awful place!

01:05:45.609 --> 01:05:47.861
(grunting)

01:05:49.905 --> 01:05:52.991
Come on, I have to get home!

01:05:55.118 --> 01:05:59.331
We'll go home together.

01:06:02.793 --> 01:06:03.627
Peter!

01:06:05.879 --> 01:06:07.172
Are you okay?

01:06:08.340 --> 01:06:12.010
(laughs) Let's go home, shall we?

01:06:12.094 --> 01:06:14.429
All of us together.

01:06:17.265 --> 01:06:19.768
Right, let's see now.

01:06:20.769 --> 01:06:23.313
Mary, how did you get here?

01:06:23.397 --> 01:06:26.483
Me? I rode a broomstick.

01:06:26.566 --> 01:06:30.612
Broomstick?
You saying you can use magic?

01:06:30.696 --> 01:06:34.574
Ah, yeah, but only for tonight.

01:06:38.870 --> 01:06:41.331
That's right, tonight.

01:06:41.415 --> 01:06:43.750
I really am a witch.

01:06:43.834 --> 01:06:45.836
Peter:
Eh?

01:06:51.007 --> 01:06:55.721
More acceleration. I need those children
in the laboratory at once.

01:06:57.556 --> 01:07:01.893
I mistrust that Mary Smith
with every atom of my body.

01:07:01.977 --> 01:07:07.149
Mary: Let me see now,
spell to unfasten locks, no, no.

01:07:07.232 --> 01:07:11.111
-You can read this?
-To smash a door down.

01:07:11.194 --> 01:07:13.447
No, we need something
that will change everyone back.

01:07:13.530 --> 01:07:16.199
Peter:
Just by chanting a spell?

01:07:16.283 --> 01:07:20.078
I don't think any one can just chant that,
you have to have some power.

01:07:20.162 --> 01:07:23.498
So this power of yours, when did you
figure out you first had it?

01:07:23.582 --> 01:07:27.627
Ah, I found it!
The spell to undo all magic.

01:07:27.711 --> 01:07:31.465
"What's done is done until it's undone."

01:07:35.802 --> 01:07:37.971
(yelping)

01:07:41.224 --> 01:07:42.517
Mary!

01:07:45.854 --> 01:07:47.439
Mary, what's happening?

01:08:03.747 --> 01:08:06.666
-Peter: Gib!
-(meowing)

01:08:15.175 --> 01:08:16.384
Mary!

01:08:16.468 --> 01:08:18.386
Tib! Gib!

01:08:19.471 --> 01:08:23.141
What did you do? What's going on?

01:08:23.225 --> 01:08:25.519
If I was able to undo
the transformation spells,

01:08:25.602 --> 01:08:27.729
it should've worked on the doors too.

01:08:27.813 --> 01:08:29.356
Come on, Peter, let's go.

01:08:30.649 --> 01:08:31.566
Oh, okay.

01:08:36.696 --> 01:08:39.991
(animals growling, bellowing)

01:08:40.075 --> 01:08:42.869
-What's that?
-(banging)

01:08:46.456 --> 01:08:48.208
(growls)

01:08:50.919 --> 01:08:54.005
(animals screeching)

01:08:57.217 --> 01:09:01.012
We might get trampled here.
Best to get out of the way.

01:09:01.680 --> 01:09:04.057
(roaring)

01:09:04.140 --> 01:09:07.769
How can my magical locks be broken?

01:09:07.853 --> 01:09:12.816
It's impossible! I cast the spell myself!

01:09:12.899 --> 01:09:14.734
No, no!

01:09:23.285 --> 01:09:27.414
-(rumbling)
-Who could that be?

01:09:27.497 --> 01:09:29.624
(gasps)

01:09:34.462 --> 01:09:36.882
How could this have happened?

01:09:41.720 --> 01:09:43.805
Reveal not conceal!

01:09:43.889 --> 01:09:44.890
(shrieks)

01:09:44.973 --> 01:09:49.436
My book of master spells!

01:09:57.277 --> 01:10:00.196
Yes, look, the door's open, Mary!

01:10:01.948 --> 01:10:03.283
I'm over here.

01:10:05.410 --> 01:10:07.412
(animals growling, bellowing)

01:10:23.219 --> 01:10:25.138
-Where to now?
-There!

01:10:30.727 --> 01:10:34.064
-Do you think they know the way out?
-Let's follow them.

01:10:43.657 --> 01:10:44.616
(shouts)

01:10:46.117 --> 01:10:49.496
(Mary and Peter shouting)

01:10:49.746 --> 01:10:51.915
(panting)

01:10:57.337 --> 01:11:00.757
Peter!
What are they doing?

01:11:01.883 --> 01:11:05.136
Clearly they tried to escape,
but how have they done this?

01:11:05.220 --> 01:11:09.224
That girl, Dr. Dee,
she stole the master spell book!

01:11:09.307 --> 01:11:11.101
After them!

01:11:22.570 --> 01:11:25.323
Okay, we can do this,
I know we can, ready?

01:11:25.407 --> 01:11:26.658
-Wait!
-Come on!

01:11:26.741 --> 01:11:30.537
-There must be another way.
-Flanagan: Hey, new girl!

01:11:33.081 --> 01:11:34.374
Little broomstick!

01:11:34.457 --> 01:11:38.628
What did I say about leaving
this little fellow all over the place?

01:11:38.712 --> 01:11:41.548
I told you to put it away with the others.

01:11:41.631 --> 01:11:43.591
Mr. Flanagan.

01:11:43.675 --> 01:11:46.469
You need to have more
respect for your broom.

01:11:46.553 --> 01:11:51.641
Young folk, these days.
And what is going on today?

01:11:51.725 --> 01:11:53.268
Thank you, Mr. Flanagan!

01:11:57.772 --> 01:12:00.817
-Flanagan!
-Ah, he'll never change.

01:12:03.778 --> 01:12:05.155
-Get on.
-Huh?

01:12:05.238 --> 01:12:07.073
Do as I say.

01:12:14.164 --> 01:12:18.001
-We're floating.
-Hold on, will you?

01:12:19.294 --> 01:12:23.298
Grab, attack, bring them back!

01:12:26.593 --> 01:12:29.095
(Peter yelping)

01:12:29.179 --> 01:12:32.098
-Peter!
-(grunting)

01:12:37.562 --> 01:12:40.982
-Mary, go on, get out of here.
-What?

01:12:41.066 --> 01:12:43.985
-Go!
-No! Peter!

01:12:55.121 --> 01:12:57.874
Dr. Dee:
A perfect young specimen.

01:12:57.957 --> 01:13:02.128
You're going to be the subject
of my most important magical experiment.

01:13:02.212 --> 01:13:04.672
You should be thrilled.

01:13:05.840 --> 01:13:08.468
(Peter shouts)

01:13:08.551 --> 01:13:10.470
Leave me alone.

01:13:13.681 --> 01:13:17.811
Now I must retrieve my master spells
from that impostor witch.

01:13:17.894 --> 01:13:21.981
That girl could ruin everything and then
we'll never get another chance.

01:13:25.735 --> 01:13:28.488
Go back, I said go back!

01:13:28.571 --> 01:13:32.909
Why won't you do what I say,
little broomstick, why?

01:13:45.797 --> 01:13:47.799
Where are you taking me?

01:13:50.009 --> 01:13:54.889
-Down there?
-(broomstick mumbles)

01:13:54.973 --> 01:13:56.558
Oh, hang on, Tib!

01:13:56.641 --> 01:13:58.977
(screaming)

01:14:03.523 --> 01:14:05.775
(grunting)

01:14:13.032 --> 01:14:14.534
Oh, what was that?

01:14:16.119 --> 01:14:17.620
Little broomstick?

01:14:37.765 --> 01:14:39.767
I wonder who lives here?

01:14:44.189 --> 01:14:47.108
Light Fairy: Welcome home, miss.
Nice to see you.

01:14:47.192 --> 01:14:50.111
-This isn't my...
-(creaks)

01:14:56.618 --> 01:14:57.869
Wow.

01:15:06.878 --> 01:15:12.467
This is your home?
So when I said go back, you--

01:15:14.344 --> 01:15:17.805
Light Fairy: It's been such a long time
since you've been home.

01:15:17.889 --> 01:15:20.350
Truly overjoyed to see you again.

01:15:20.433 --> 01:15:23.561
In fact, I didn't think
you were ever coming back.

01:15:23.645 --> 01:15:25.813
Now everything's ready,
please come inside.

01:15:28.858 --> 01:15:30.193
Hello?

01:15:35.240 --> 01:15:37.784
What a lovely room.

01:15:54.342 --> 01:15:56.010
Oh my goodness.

01:15:58.137 --> 01:16:00.139
Photos.

01:16:03.017 --> 01:16:06.771
(gasps) It's Madam and Dr. Dee.

01:16:06.854 --> 01:16:09.274
(Tib growls)

01:16:10.900 --> 01:16:12.986
Tibu! What is it?

01:16:13.069 --> 01:16:15.571
Careful, don't touch anything.

01:16:16.072 --> 01:16:17.448
Look.

01:16:19.575 --> 01:16:22.328
This is how they transformed Gib.

01:16:22.412 --> 01:16:24.789
Awful, how dare they do this.

01:16:27.959 --> 01:16:30.837
What is this?

01:16:36.801 --> 01:16:40.513
They want to transform people.

01:16:41.931 --> 01:16:43.683
-Woman: Mary?
-(gasps)

01:16:43.766 --> 01:16:46.185
I'm sorry.

01:16:51.107 --> 01:16:53.109
It's just my reflection.

01:17:00.325 --> 01:17:02.285
Is someone there?

01:17:07.957 --> 01:17:09.042
Mary.

01:17:09.709 --> 01:17:12.378
Great Aunt Charlotte,
I don't understand.

01:17:12.462 --> 01:17:14.714
You're in my old house, my dear.

01:17:14.797 --> 01:17:18.092
My little broomstick
must've brought you to it.

01:17:18.176 --> 01:17:21.220
Mary: Your home, your broomstick,
what do you mean?

01:17:21.304 --> 01:17:24.390
Mary, the flower,
where is the fly-by-night?

01:17:24.474 --> 01:17:28.478
Mary: I don't know,
Madam and Dr. Dee took it.

01:17:28.561 --> 01:17:32.523
-Oh Madam, Dr. Dee.
-Wait, Great Aunt Charlotte--

01:17:32.607 --> 01:17:38.696
Mary, please listen, those two are trying
to do something extremely dangerous.

01:17:41.449 --> 01:17:43.618
(yelping)

01:17:46.954 --> 01:17:48.748
What's happened?

01:17:48.831 --> 01:17:51.167
Once I was a student here.

01:17:52.043 --> 01:17:55.546
I stole the fly-by-night seeds
and escaped.

01:17:55.630 --> 01:17:57.048
You stole them?

01:18:02.553 --> 01:18:06.099
Charlotte: Back then Madam and Dr. Dee
were loved by everyone.

01:18:06.182 --> 01:18:10.144
They were very gifted scientists
and kind-hearted teachers.

01:18:13.314 --> 01:18:17.151
But one day, I, like you, came across
the fly-by-night in the woods.

01:18:17.235 --> 01:18:19.237
I made the mistake of giving it to them.

01:18:23.116 --> 01:18:25.993
They were never the same again.

01:18:31.040 --> 01:18:36.504
They became obsessed
with the fly-by-night.

01:18:37.422 --> 01:18:40.675
Spending endless hours studying the seeds
that would bear the flowers.

01:18:40.758 --> 01:18:43.678
Madam saw the potential
of the fly-by-night

01:18:43.761 --> 01:18:46.264
to transform students
so they would be able

01:18:46.347 --> 01:18:49.183
to wield infinite magical ability.

01:18:54.689 --> 01:18:58.651
But the experiment ended in tragedy.
They simply couldn't control its power.

01:19:00.945 --> 01:19:03.156
I had no choice, I had to do something.

01:19:03.239 --> 01:19:05.741
I couldn't let them make
the same mistake again.

01:19:07.910 --> 01:19:11.914
In this world, there exists certain powers
that can never be harnessed.

01:19:11.998 --> 01:19:16.335
Yet despite everything that happened,

01:19:16.419 --> 01:19:22.592
those two still believe that
the experiment can work.

01:19:22.675 --> 01:19:26.387
And if they have the flower
that means they'll be able to...

01:19:32.727 --> 01:19:35.938
Mary:
They're going to try it again on Peter.

01:19:37.607 --> 01:19:40.568
Charlotte:
Mary, put your hand on the mirror.

01:19:40.651 --> 01:19:42.945
Mary:
Like this?

01:19:43.029 --> 01:19:45.323
It's been a long time
since I've done magic,

01:19:45.406 --> 01:19:48.075
but perhaps I can get this to you.

01:19:55.416 --> 01:19:59.128
-The flower!
-It's the last one.

01:19:59.212 --> 01:20:02.423
Mary, you don't have much
magical power left in you.

01:20:02.507 --> 01:20:04.717
Use that flower to come home at once.

01:20:04.800 --> 01:20:08.513
Otherwise you won't be able
to return home ever again.

01:20:08.596 --> 01:20:10.598
Do you understand, Mary?

01:20:28.157 --> 01:20:30.826
No, I can't just come home by myself.

01:20:30.910 --> 01:20:34.830
I made a promise that
we'd come home together.

01:20:34.914 --> 01:20:36.832
I must go to Peter.

01:20:36.916 --> 01:20:38.251
Peter?

01:20:38.334 --> 01:20:41.963
If this is the last flower,
I have to use it to save him.

01:20:44.298 --> 01:20:45.550
Mary!

01:20:48.302 --> 01:20:49.845
Mary:
It's Madam.

01:20:50.137 --> 01:20:53.349
Mary, I wish I could do
more for you, but I can't.

01:20:53.432 --> 01:20:57.770
You won't have much
power, dear, are you sure?

01:20:57.853 --> 01:21:01.691
I made a promise to Peter
and I will be coming back with him.

01:21:01.774 --> 01:21:03.442
Mary.

01:21:06.070 --> 01:21:07.446
Mary.

01:21:12.368 --> 01:21:15.121
Now why on earth would she come here?

01:21:15.204 --> 01:21:17.832
(broom mumbles)

01:21:19.000 --> 01:21:20.501
Oh, no you don't!

01:21:22.962 --> 01:21:24.130
Ready to go?

01:21:26.716 --> 01:21:28.217
Little broomstick.

01:21:31.262 --> 01:21:32.346
Are you okay?

01:21:33.723 --> 01:21:35.725
(yelps)

01:21:42.148 --> 01:21:43.190
No!

01:21:45.484 --> 01:21:47.653
Grab, attack, bring her back.

01:21:54.410 --> 01:21:57.038
Little broomstick, hang in there.

01:21:57.121 --> 01:21:58.998
Take me to Peter!

01:22:01.459 --> 01:22:03.294
She still has power.

01:22:04.295 --> 01:22:06.505
After her.

01:22:10.801 --> 01:22:13.596
That must be where they're keeping him.

01:22:13.679 --> 01:22:15.431
At last, it begins.

01:22:22.146 --> 01:22:26.067
Grab, attack, steal it back.

01:22:32.031 --> 01:22:33.115
My bag!

01:22:36.577 --> 01:22:37.828
And the flower!

01:22:41.457 --> 01:22:42.625
Give it back!

01:22:42.708 --> 01:22:45.586
Foolish girl, the book and the flower
belong to me in the first place.

01:22:45.670 --> 01:22:47.838
You have no claim on them.

01:22:47.922 --> 01:22:51.759
Fly, seek, pursue, stick to her like glue.

01:22:59.725 --> 01:23:01.894
(grunting)

01:23:07.525 --> 01:23:10.945
She'll have to use up all
the power she has left.

01:23:11.028 --> 01:23:17.952
And to think she had one last flower
up her sleeve, terrifying.

01:23:20.913 --> 01:23:24.291
(broom mumbles)

01:23:24.375 --> 01:23:27.461
Please hold on, just a little bit longer.

01:23:27.545 --> 01:23:29.797
(shouting)

01:23:31.507 --> 01:23:33.008
Little broomstick!

01:23:51.193 --> 01:23:53.446
(groaning)

01:24:00.411 --> 01:24:03.330
-Out of power.
-(Tib meows)

01:24:04.874 --> 01:24:06.125
Tib!

01:24:11.630 --> 01:24:13.132
Little broomstick!

01:24:15.217 --> 01:24:16.260
No!

01:24:17.094 --> 01:24:19.013
Please say something.

01:24:20.264 --> 01:24:21.766
Little broomstick.

01:24:24.143 --> 01:24:26.812
What am I going to do now?

01:24:26.896 --> 01:24:29.064
(sobbing)

01:24:39.283 --> 01:24:41.285
Little broomstick.

01:24:44.455 --> 01:24:46.791
(meows)

01:24:51.837 --> 01:24:53.881
You're right.

01:24:55.174 --> 01:24:57.301
I mustn't give up.

01:25:03.349 --> 01:25:05.851
I made a promise.

01:25:10.272 --> 01:25:13.567
We are going home together, all of us.

01:25:21.242 --> 01:25:24.161
(thunder rumbling)

01:26:02.283 --> 01:26:04.535
(shouting)

01:26:12.751 --> 01:26:15.337
It's you, you're from the strongroom.

01:26:15.421 --> 01:26:18.507
(animals screeching)

01:27:06.722 --> 01:27:08.641
There's no other way.

01:27:08.724 --> 01:27:11.936
Thanks I'll go on alone from here.

01:27:14.104 --> 01:27:15.773
Good bye.

01:27:17.232 --> 01:27:21.904
I couldn't have made it this far
without you, thank you.

01:27:23.405 --> 01:27:26.116
I'm coming, Peter.

01:27:39.838 --> 01:27:41.256
What now?

01:27:41.340 --> 01:27:44.009
(Tib and Gib meow)

01:27:50.307 --> 01:27:51.725
Gib, you're safe!

01:27:53.686 --> 01:27:57.022
I'm so glad. Where's Peter?

01:28:00.901 --> 01:28:02.820
In there, are you sure?

01:28:10.911 --> 01:28:13.497
(low groaning)

01:28:29.013 --> 01:28:32.433
I told you before, in the Velta socket.

01:28:36.103 --> 01:28:39.231
(electricity zapping)

01:28:42.776 --> 01:28:44.570
The fly-by-night.

01:28:44.653 --> 01:28:49.241
All is ready, the final stage
of the transformation experiment.

01:28:51.118 --> 01:28:58.000
We stand on the cusp of magical history.

01:29:04.298 --> 01:29:05.340
Peter!

01:29:06.383 --> 01:29:12.639
Mumblechook: Soon this boy will possess
the ability to wield any magic.

01:29:12.723 --> 01:29:15.768
He will be changed forever.

01:29:15.851 --> 01:29:18.937
Dr. Dee:
And then we shall change the world.

01:29:19.021 --> 01:29:21.023
Stop it!

01:29:33.827 --> 01:29:36.038
It is simply superb.

01:29:36.121 --> 01:29:37.664
Peter!

01:29:37.748 --> 01:29:40.501
Please, stop it! Please, you must!

01:29:43.545 --> 01:29:44.880
Dr. Dee!

01:29:47.049 --> 01:29:50.052
(explosion booming)

01:29:51.095 --> 01:29:52.554
It can't be.

01:29:53.972 --> 01:29:56.225
(burbling)

01:29:57.351 --> 01:30:01.396
-Peter.
-Dr. Dee: Calm down, everyone.

01:30:01.480 --> 01:30:04.441
This is no failure, this is rebirth.

01:30:04.525 --> 01:30:06.944
The egg has merely cracked, but... Hmm?

01:30:09.696 --> 01:30:12.449
(yelps) Doctor, it's melting!

01:30:13.826 --> 01:30:16.370
This can't be happening!
Open the valve!

01:30:21.416 --> 01:30:22.334
No!

01:30:25.045 --> 01:30:26.964
Not yet, not yet!

01:30:27.047 --> 01:30:29.299
(shouting)

01:30:34.513 --> 01:30:39.476
This is a disaster!
Doctor, we must do something!

01:30:42.813 --> 01:30:46.150
-Peter: Mary.
-Peter!

01:30:46.233 --> 01:30:48.443
Don't panic, this is
merely the second stage.

01:30:48.527 --> 01:30:52.281
We can still control
the power by taking-- Aah!

01:30:52.364 --> 01:30:54.366
(Mumblechook screams)

01:31:02.457 --> 01:31:04.626
(zapping)

01:31:12.926 --> 01:31:15.596
Dr. Dee:
This is just like the last time.

01:31:17.306 --> 01:31:21.476
-Doctor, we must undo everything.
-No, you mustn't!

01:31:25.314 --> 01:31:27.691
We have to stop this now!

01:31:27.774 --> 01:31:29.651
Madam, be careful!

01:31:29.735 --> 01:31:33.238
Dr. Dee:
Don't, all our work will be for nothing!

01:31:38.410 --> 01:31:40.829
(growling)

01:31:40.913 --> 01:31:41.872
Madam!

01:31:46.752 --> 01:31:49.463
(groans)

01:31:49.546 --> 01:31:54.718
-Madam!
-The creature's drained all her magic.

01:31:57.846 --> 01:32:02.517
How has this happened?
I did everything perfectly.

01:32:13.237 --> 01:32:15.239
(meowing)

01:32:20.244 --> 01:32:22.454
(growling)

01:32:45.143 --> 01:32:46.728
There's one left.

01:32:52.943 --> 01:32:55.028
(grunts)

01:33:03.495 --> 01:33:07.124
Peter, I'm coming to rescue you!

01:33:20.053 --> 01:33:22.264
-Mary! I'm here!
-Peter!

01:33:25.309 --> 01:33:27.394
-Run!
-Peter!

01:33:27.477 --> 01:33:28.645
Dr. Dee:
Mary!

01:33:29.730 --> 01:33:32.524
Get away, Mary, before it's too late!

01:33:32.607 --> 01:33:36.278
You can't defeat it.
That creature can use any magic!

01:33:36.361 --> 01:33:39.573
It can use any magic.

01:33:39.656 --> 01:33:41.199
Peter!

01:33:44.745 --> 01:33:47.289
Peter, can you hear me?

01:33:47.372 --> 01:33:54.254
Give me your hand! You can use the book!

01:33:54.671 --> 01:33:57.382
Let's go home together.

01:33:58.425 --> 01:34:00.677
(grunting)

01:34:09.311 --> 01:34:12.439
What's done is done until it's undone!

01:34:22.866 --> 01:34:25.118
(shouting)

01:34:26.703 --> 01:34:27.704
Madam!

01:34:28.830 --> 01:34:30.665
We don't need magic!

01:35:29.182 --> 01:35:30.600
Huh?

01:35:32.686 --> 01:35:34.855
-Mary!
-Peter!

01:35:34.938 --> 01:35:37.816
And Gib, you're all right.

01:35:37.899 --> 01:35:39.651
Tib!

01:35:40.944 --> 01:35:44.156
Look, I found your bag, but, um,

01:35:44.239 --> 01:35:48.326
I have no idea where
your broomstick could be.

01:35:48.410 --> 01:35:51.788
Don't worry about it, it's fine.

01:35:51.872 --> 01:35:54.875
So how are we going to get home?

01:35:54.958 --> 01:35:58.420
Right that's it, this is
the final straw, new girl.

01:35:58.503 --> 01:36:01.590
What on earth did you do to your broom?

01:36:01.673 --> 01:36:03.884
-Mr. Flanagan.
-I remember you.

01:36:03.967 --> 01:36:06.553
Look now, it's your mistress.

01:36:07.888 --> 01:36:12.893
Hey look at that, little
broomstick, you're fixed.

01:36:14.352 --> 01:36:17.481
Of course, you really
must show more love

01:36:17.564 --> 01:36:19.566
for your broom!

01:36:19.649 --> 01:36:21.818
Thank you, Mr. Flanagan!

01:36:25.030 --> 01:36:26.198
(chuckles)

01:36:32.204 --> 01:36:35.999
Mary:
I wonder what will happen to them.

01:36:36.082 --> 01:36:40.921
Peter: Madam and Doctor Dee?
They'll be fine.

01:36:41.004 --> 01:36:44.841
After all, they can use magic.

01:36:47.135 --> 01:36:52.307
(chuckles) I guess, one day
of magic was enough for me.

01:36:52.390 --> 01:36:55.727
Hey, you've got something in your hair.

01:36:58.939 --> 01:37:00.607
Huh, look at that.

01:37:03.818 --> 01:37:06.988
Well, I won't be needing this anymore.

01:37:12.744 --> 01:37:14.621
Wait, what was that?

01:37:14.704 --> 01:37:16.623
Hold on tight, this is the last time

01:37:16.706 --> 01:37:18.833
I'm ever using magic.

01:37:18.917 --> 01:37:21.169
(shouting)

01:37:39.729 --> 01:37:43.567
(singing in Japanese)

01:37:43.650 --> 01:37:47.404
Based on "The Little Broomstick"
by Mary Stewart

01:42:35.900 --> 01:42:38.903
The End
